**Plan, nothing changed yet.**

The split is already right. `buildRows()` in [src/report.js:11](src/report.js:11) makes the data. `toTable()` in [src/format.js:14](src/format.js:14) only prints. So `--json` is a new printer plus a flag.

One call to make: the table drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose, per the note at [src/format.js:3](src/format.js:3). I would have JSON print all six fields from `buildRows()`. That is "same data" in the true sense. Say the word if you want the four table columns instead.

```js
// format.js
function toJson(rows) { return JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2); }

// cli.js
const json = argv.includes('--json');
const args = argv.filter((a) => a !== '--json');
if (args[0] !== 'report') { /* usage, 1 */ }
process.stdout.write((json ? toJson : toTable)(buildRows()) + '\n');
```

Also update `USAGE` to `report [--json]`, and reject unknown flags.

Next: say go, and which field set you want.
